{{Quote|I don't understand. What is this place?''"<br />"''Unlike any other. A conduit through which the entire Force of the universe flows.|Obi-Wan Kenobi and the vision of [[Qui-Gon Jinn]]|<ref name="Overlords" />}}
'''Mortis''' was an ethereal realm within [[the Force]] that resembled a [[planet]]. Its existence was whispered over in legends and stories passed down through the millennia by [[Jedi]], [[Sith]], and the average [[spacer]] alike. It was believed to have existed outside any [[star system]], and potentially [[the galaxy]] or even [[Universe|the universe]]. Some believed that the origins of the Force came from Mortis.

==Description==
{{Quote|Have you noticed the seasons seem to change with the time of day?''"<br />"''Yeah.|Obi-Wan Kenobi and Anakin Skywalker|<ref name="Overlords" />}}
[[File:MortisNight-Transformations.png|thumb|left|250px|Mortis after nightfall]]
Mortis was a realm of [[the Force]] that resembled a planet. Containing dreamlike environments; Mortis could not be mapped, and the landscape changed frequently, with even landmarks appearing in different locations frequently. The daytime was a time of peace during which blossomed lush fields, [[Color|green]] [[mountain]]s, and stunning vistas. Dense [[forest]]s, [[Magma|molten]] [[cave]]rns, and floating mountains above the surface were among some of the different biospheres. The light had a healing quality, although it came from no star. When night fell, the [[plant]]s withered and died, the creatures vanished, and the few stars that shone in the black sky were unidentifiable. Scalding [[Water|rains]] swept the terrain, making survival without shelter nearly impossible.<ref name="NoP" />

Entrance to the mysterious [[planet]] was never voluntary, as Mortis drew in its visitors inexplicably. It manifested itself in different ways; Mortis was reported as having appeared as a massive [[Mortis monolith|monolith]] floating in [[Realspace|space]], serving as a portal into the realm. In other times individuals walked through a door or landed there without discernible reason. Time within Mortis had no meaning; what seemed like days or weeks within the realm, passed within seconds outside of the realm,<ref name="NoP" /> a mysterious quality it shared with such locales as [[Ahch-To]] and [[Dagobah]].<ref name="TLJVD">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

==Inhabitants==
{{Quote|My children and I can manipulate the Force like no other.|The Father, the patriarch of a family of Force wielders|<ref name="Overlords" />}}
The realm of Mortis was inhabited by only three intelligent beings, [[Force wielder]]s locked in an eternal struggle for dominance over one another: the [[Son]], who represented the destructive and deadly aspects of the realm and was aligned with the [[dark side of the Force]]; the [[Daughter]], who represented peace and creation on Mortis and was aligned with the [[light side of the Force]]; and the [[Father (Mortis)|Father]], who maintained the balance of the Force between the two.<ref name="MortisSWE" /> Mortis was therefore a fulcrum for [[the galaxy]] and an extremely powerful conduit through which the Force flowed.<ref name="Overlords" />

==History==
{{Quote|When news reached me that the chosen one had been found, I needed to see for myself.''"<br />"''The chosen one is a myth.''"<br />"''Is it? I should very much like to know. Why don't we find out together? Pass one test, and I shall know the truth. Then you and your friends may leave.|The Father and Anakin Skywalker|<ref name="Overlords" />}}
[[File:MortisDay-Transformations.png|thumb|right|250px|Mortis during the day]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], the Father drew [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], and [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] into the realm from the [[Chrelythiumn system]].<ref name="Overlords" /> The Father realized that Skywalker was the prophesized [[Chosen One]], and that he could maintain the balance of the Force between the two children once the Father [[Death|died]].<ref name="MortisSWE" /> This led to a struggle between the Force wielders and the three [[Jedi]], culminating in the deaths of all three wielders and the restoration of balance on Mortis.<ref name="Ghosts of Mortis" />

The ethereal realm shared its name with the [[Phases of Mortis]], a solution to the [[Unsolved Theorem of Master Thorpe]] that was included in the [[sacred Jedi texts]].<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Mortis first appeared in the episodes "[[Overlords]]," "[[Altar of Mortis (episode)|Altar of Mortis]]," and [[Ghosts of Mortis]]" in the [[The Clone Wars: Season Three|third season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''.<ref name="Overlords" /> It was later mentioned in the ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'' episodes "[[Wolves and a Door]]" and "[[A World Between Worlds]]," with the Mortis gods also pertaining to the mysterious and mystical plane known as the [[World Between Worlds]].<ref name="Wolves and a Door">{{Rebels|Wolves and a Door}}</ref><ref name="A World Between Worlds">{{Rebels|A World Between Worlds}}</ref>

